From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] explorer, mountmgr: a USB drive that arrives gets a notification that opens it

As Windows' AutoPlay: a USB drive or a disc arriving brings up a
notification, "SGSTICK (E:) -- Select to open it in File Explorer", and
selecting it opens the drive there (David 2026-10-01: plugging a USB drive
did nothing). It is a tray icon of its own with a balloon, gone after 15
seconds, when used, or when the drive goes.

Three things in the way:
 * the shell's taskbar never showed any tray balloon: show_balloon asked
   for the stand-alone tray (show_systray), which the taskbar mode turns
   off;
 * a balloon asked for with the icon (NIM_ADD with NIF_INFO) was refused
   while the icon was not yet shown, and never asked for again;
 * the tray told a balloon's owner nothing: now NIN_BALLOONSHOW,
   NIN_BALLOONUSERCLICK (a click on it) and NIN_BALLOONTIMEOUT, as on
   Windows.
And mount manager gave a USB stick (removable, no known media) no drive
type, so it was a fixed disk (GetDriveType 3); it is a removable disk now
(2), as on Windows.
